seq_run.py — host-side runner for the on-chip command sequencer (rung 1).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --prefix PREFIX       <prefix>.seq / .seqdata.bin / .seq.json
  --base BASE           generator-artifact prefix (.weights.json, _w*.bin,
                        .emb.bin); default = --prefix minus its last dotted
                        component
  --dev DEV
  --chan CHAN           DDR FETCH channel (stream/blob/emb); must match the
                        emitter's chan
  --four-chan           require a row-split (meta nch>1) stream: weights are
                        split across DDR channels 0..nch-1 and each quarter is
                        readback-verified where its matvec_chan reads it. The
                        mode is otherwise auto-detected from meta['nch']; this
                        flag just asserts it.
  --dry-run             plan + relocate + upload + readback-verify, and
                        NOTHING ELSE — no access at all to the SEQ CSR window,
                        so this is the mode that is safe on a bitstream
                        without seq_0
  --skip-weights        weights + embedding are already resident
  --no-verify           skip the DDR readback comparison
  --zero-scratch        write zeros over the 32K layer_chan scratchpad
                        (SPTR/SWIN, idle-only) before starting, and read it
                        back to prove it cleared. The FPGA never clears the
                        pad between runs while ref/seq_model's memory is zero-
                        initialised, so a word this stream does not write
                        shows the PREVIOUS model's leftovers and the .chip
                        golden calls it a mismatch. Harmless while one
                        geometry owns the board; required when 0.8B and 2B
                        alternate
                        (evidence/qwen2b/rd/hw_22_scratch_residue_proof.log)
  --no-xrf-init         do not zero XRF[0..7] before START
  --entry ENTRY
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --chip CHIP           post-halt golden from
                        tb/scripts/gen_seq_chip_vectors.py (default
                        <prefix>.chip)
  --no-chip
  --dump-scratch DUMP_SCRATCH
                        save the post-halt 16K scratchpad to a .npy
  --out OUT             JSON report path
  --selftest            unit-test the pure-python pieces (no board)
  --expect-version HASH
                        the resident sequencer bitstream's VERSION (8-hex git
                        hash), when it is NOT the shipped c973c18a: e.g.
                        9b588e78 for build_042_bm1. Must be a row of
                        SEQ_VERSIONS. Default: $FABLE5_SEQ_EXPECT_VERSION if
                        set, else EXPECTED_SEQ_VERSION
  --lock LOCK           the shared board lock (default
                        /home/cah/r2d2/code/fpga/.fable5_board.lock;
                        $FABLE5_BOARD_LOCK overrides the default)
  --no-lock             run WITHOUT the board lock. For a human who has
                        confirmed sole use of the board; never for a script,
                        and never to get past a stuck lock. Logged loudly on
                        stdout, stderr and <lock>.nolock.log
